IMPORT prelude

-- Salvation Army Ordinance 1939 (Singapore) -- the General of the Salvation Army as a corporation sole (s 2), the movable property it
-- took over from Evangeline Booth (s 3), what it may acquire and dispose of (ss 4, 5), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 6),
-- suing it and serving it (s 7), a change of General (s 8), what proves who the General is (s 9), the General's Attorney (s 10), and whose
-- rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation "version in force from 1/4/2022", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SAO1939.txt. The deposit says the Revised Edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amendment annotated is "[Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]"
-- under s 7 (the Courts (Civil and Criminal Justice) Reform Act 2021, per the Legislative History); the only other annotation is "[7/97]"
-- under s 11. The Ordinance is Ordinance 23 of 1939, published 15 September 1939.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0248 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- Ordinance is eleven sections long, so the whole of it is in scope except the short title. For a person outside the Salvation Army it
-- matters when buying from, leasing from or lending to the Corporation (ss 5, 6), when suing it (s 7), and when checking who may act for
-- it (ss 9, 10).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the recitals (the Deeds of Constitution of 1878, 1904 and 1930), except as background; the content of
-- s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 6(1) refers (whether a power of attorney was "deposited" under it is a
-- stated fact); what "the like extent" in s 3 amounts to; what a "restraint, reservation or condition" in an acquisition document says
-- (s 5; its presence is a stated fact); other modes of service besides the one s 7 provides; the Salvation Army's internal governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Salvation Army Ordinance 1939 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 and 9 -- who the Corporation is, and what proves who the General is`

-- s 2(1): "The General of the Salvation Army for the time being shall be deemed a corporation sole (hereinafter called 'the Corporation')
-- and shall be known and described as 'The General of the Salvation Army'", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 9: "Upon the lodging at the office of the Minister of a copy or copies certified by the Chief of the Staff of the Salvation Army or the
-- Commissioner acting for the time being as the Chief of the Staff ... of a document or documents purporting to be or to record the
-- appointment of and acceptance of office by a General of the Salvation Army it shall be deemed to be conclusive in evidence that the
-- person named in such certified copy or copies is the person duly authorised to exercise the office of the General for the time being
-- ... until the recording and lodging of a similarly certified copy or copies as aforesaid."
--
-- Four things are needed: a lodged copy naming the person, certification by the Chief of the Staff or the acting Commissioner, a document
-- recording both appointment AND acceptance of office, and no later similarly certified copy lodged. The conclusive effect runs "until"
-- the next lodging, not until the General's term ends: a General who has left office stays, in evidence, the General until a successor's
-- papers are lodged (the plain words; no case was read).
DECLARE Certifier IS ONE OF
    `the Chief of the Staff`
    `the Commissioner acting as Chief of the Staff`
    `a notary public`
    `a territorial commander`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is named in a copy lodged at the office of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lodged copy is certified by` IS A Certifier
    `the document records appointment and acceptance of office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a later similarly certified copy has been lodged` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the certifier` IS A Certifier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a certifier section 9 accepts` IF
    CONSIDER `the certifier`
    WHEN `the Chief of the Staff` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commissioner acting as Chief of the Staff` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is conclusively the General in evidence` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is named in a copy lodged at the office of the Minister`
    AND `is a certifier section 9 accepts` (`the claimant`'s `the lodged copy is certified by`)
    AND `the claimant`'s `the document records appointment and acceptance of office`
    AND (NOT `the claimant`'s `a later similarly certified copy has been lodged`)

§§ `3 and 8 -- property vested in the Corporation, and a change of General`

-- s 3: "All movable property in this Colony now vested in the said Evangeline Booth is hereby vested in the Corporation to the like extent
-- to which the same vested in the said Evangeline Booth prior to 15 September 1939."
-- s 8: "No change of the person holding the office of General ... shall affect any immovable or movable property or any interest therein
-- vested in the Corporation but the same shall notwithstanding any such change continue to be vested in the Corporation."
--
-- s 3 sweeps in movable property only. The recitals explain why: Evangeline Booth held movables, and immovable property was still "to be
-- so acquired". "This Colony" is the 1939 wording kept in the 2020 Revised Edition; reading it as Singapore today is an inference.
DECLARE Item HAS
    `is movable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in this Colony` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was vested in Evangeline Booth before 15 September 1939` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 vests it in the Corporation` IF
        `the item`'s `is movable`
    AND `the item`'s `is in this Colony`
    AND `the item`'s `was vested in Evangeline Booth before 15 September 1939`

GIVEN `was vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person holding the office of General has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is still vested in the Corporation` IF
    `was vested in the Corporation`

§§ `4, 5 and 7 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 4: "full power to acquire by purchase, transfer, donation, exchange, devise, bequest, grant, gift, conveyance, or otherwise any
-- immovable or movable property in this Colony or any estate or interest therein."
-- s 5: "subject to any restraint, reservation or condition contained in the document under which it shall acquire title thereto have full
-- power and be entitled to sell, mortgage, lease, exchange, partition, or otherwise dispose of and deal with all property ... which may for
-- the time being be vested in or have been acquired by it under any of the provisions of this Ordinance."
-- s 7: "The Corporation may sue and be sued and take all legal proceedings in any of the Courts of the Colony".
--
-- Disposal reaches only property vested in or acquired by the Corporation, and yields to a restraint in the title document. The power to
-- sue and be sued is general: unlike some other incorporation ordinances, it is not confined to proceedings about property. The Ordinance
-- grants nothing else (whether the general law supplies more is outside the text and not encoded).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `acquire property by purchase`
    `acquire property by devise or bequest`
    `acquire property by donation or gift`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `exchange or partition property`
    `otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue or be sued in the courts`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in or was acquired by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the title document restrains it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `acquire property by purchase` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire property by devise or bequest` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire property by donation or gift` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sue or be sued in the courts` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `borrow money without security` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the property is vested in or was acquired by the Corporation` AND (NOT `the title document restrains it`)

§§ `6 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 6(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the General for the time being of the Salvation Army or his attorney duly authorised by a power of
-- attorney deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 and shall also be signed by the General for the time
-- being or his attorney so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 6(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same is
-- the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- The attorney who may witness and sign is one whose power is DEPOSITED under s 48 of the 1886 Act. Lodging a copy at the Minister's office
-- under s 10 is a different act; s 6 does not mention it, so an attorney lodged under s 10 but not deposited under s 48 does not qualify on
-- the words. Witness and signer need not be the same person (each limb says "the General ... or his attorney"); that reading is encoded.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the General for the time being`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney lodged with the Minister but not deposited`
    `a Salvation Army officer with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the General or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the General for the time being` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 6 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the General or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the General or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the General or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `10 and 7 -- the General's Attorney, and serving the Corporation`

-- s 10: the General "shall have power to appoint an Attorney for such time and purposes and with such powers as may be stated in the power
-- of attorney and a notarially certified copy of the said power of attorney shall be lodged at the office of the Minister and the donee of
-- the said power of attorney shall be deemed to be the duly authorised Attorney of the General ... until the recording and lodging of a
-- subsequent and similarly certified copy power of attorney."
-- s 7: "all originating claims, notices and legal process may be served upon the Corporation by being left at the residence in this Colony
-- of the duly appointed Attorney of the General for the time being".
--
-- That the deeming in s 10 depends on the copy being notarially certified and lodged is a reading of the sentence (the lodging and the
-- deeming are joined by "and"), not an express condition. Reading "the duly appointed Attorney" in s 7 as the Attorney deemed under s 10 is
-- an inference. s 7 says process "may" be served this way; whether other modes are good is not addressed and not encoded.
DECLARE Attorney HAS
    `was appointed by the General by power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a notarially certified copy is lodged at the office of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a subsequent similarly certified copy has been lodged` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the attorney` IS AN Attorney
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is deemed the duly authorised Attorney` IF
        `the attorney`'s `was appointed by the General by power of attorney`
    AND `the attorney`'s `a notarially certified copy is lodged at the office of the Minister`
    AND (NOT `the attorney`'s `a subsequent similarly certified copy has been lodged`)

GIVEN `the attorney` IS AN Attorney, `was left at the residence of that attorney` IS A BOOLEAN, `the residence is in this Colony` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is service section 7 provides for` IF
        `is deemed the duly authorised Attorney` `the attorney`
    AND `was left at the residence of that attorney`
    AND `the residence is in this Colony`

§§ `11 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 11: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall prejudice or affect the right of the Government or any body politic or corporate or of any other
-- person or persons, except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from, through, or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from, through or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from, through or under a person mentioned`
